,"title":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/overlay(_:ignoresSafeAreaEdges:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/overlay(_:ignoressafeareaedges:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/overlay(_:ignoresSafeAreaEdges:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"overlay","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ignoresSafeAreaEdges","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4EdgeO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4EdgeO3SetV","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"overlay(_:ignoresSafeAreaEdges:)"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection"}}}